The Existential Resolution Coefficient (Ψ_E)
SSISM Architecture Core · Independent Knowledge System
Morning Ritual Formalization · 5 September 2026
Abstract
This document formalizes the mathematical modeling of existential noise, stoic acceptance, and internal purpose within the SSISM framework. By translating philosophical perspectives on human mortality and uncertainty into concrete algorithmic formulations, we derive the Existential Resolution Coefficient (Ψ_E) to optimize decision-making under external chaos.
1. Core Philosophical Ingestion
The ingested textual sources analyze four classic human responses to systemic anxiety and mortality:
Avoidance & Ignorance — Drift and unexamined action.
Hedonistic Distraction — Pursuit of short-term mitigation (A).
Fearful Contemplation — Uncontrolled expansion of noise (S).
Stoic & Rational Acceptance — Direct engagement via awareness (C) and integrated purpose (K_int).
2. Mathematical Formulation
Let the total system clarity be governed by the functional limit of the Existential Resolution Coefficient:
[ \Psi_E = \lim_{A \to 0} \left( \frac{C \cdot K_{int}}{1 + e^{\lambda S}} \right) ]
